<DocsLayout
  title="Keyboard shortcuts"
  description="How keyboard use works in Astrofox, and which keys are the most dependable."
>
  <p>
    Astrofox is primarily designed around visible controls in the workspace.
    Keyboard support mostly follows normal browser and form behavior, so the
    most dependable keys are the ones used for focus, dialogs, and text entry.
  </p>

  <h2>Reliable keys</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Tab</strong> - move forward through buttons, fields, and other controls.</li>
    <li><strong>Shift + Tab</strong> - move focus backward.</li>
    <li><strong>Enter</strong> - confirm the focused button or dialog action.</li>
    <li><strong>Esc</strong> - close the active dialog or cancel the current modal interaction.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Text fields</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Standard browser text editing shortcuts usually apply inside inputs.</li>
    <li>Use your platform's normal copy, paste, select-all, and cursor movement keys when editing labels or values.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Browser-level commands</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Some browsers may reserve common commands such as save, print, or find.</li>
    <li>If a keyboard combination opens a browser feature instead of an Astrofox action, use the on-screen control in the app.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Practical advice</h2>
  <p>
    For now, the best approach is to learn the visible controls first, then use
    keyboard navigation to move through forms and dialogs faster. If you are
    looking for workflow speedups, <a href="/docs/quick-start">Quick start</a>,
    <a href="/docs/reactor-recipes">Reactor recipes</a>, and
    <a href="/docs/performance">Performance tuning</a> will save more time than
    memorizing browser-dependent key combinations.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
